==============================================================
 Phase 3 demo — GB-5 spend caps, GB-6 alerts, mid-stream cut
==============================================================

The 100k-token scenario, five lines of YAML (demo/budget.yaml):

        spend_caps:
          team:
            default: 100000
            overrides:
              ml-research: 200000
              free-tier: 5000

--------------------------------------------------------------
(1)(2)(3) GB-5 default cap + GB-6 alerts + GB-4 cap rejection
--------------------------------------------------------------
team=free-tier is capped at 25 tokens for a legible demo (the same cap
machinery as the headline 100k scenario, a smaller number). Each fixture
stream is ~9 tokens, so the running tally crosses 80% then the cap; the
GB-6 soft and hard alerts fire AT the enforcement point, then the next
request is rejected at request start with the operator's GB-4 body.

  request #1 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #2 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #3 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 200
  request #4 for team=free-tier -> HTTP 429

The operator's GB-4 body on the rejected request (naming cap + spend):
$ curl -sN -X POST 'http://127.0.0.1:6188/openai/v1/chat' -H 'x-attr-team: free-tier' -d '{}'
{"error":"budget_exhausted","spender":"team=free-tier","cap_tokens":"25","spend_tokens":"28","route":"/openai"}
gatewayd enforcement log (GB-6 alerts + GB-5 budget lines) for free-tier:
    [2026-08-01T19:13:08Z INFO  gatewayd::budget] [budget /openai] team=free-tier reconciled est=10->auth=9; spent=9/25 tokens (share=25) cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z INFO  gatewayd::budget] [budget /openai] team=free-tier reconciled est=10->auth=9; spent=18/25 tokens (share=25) cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z WARN  gatewayd::budget] [gb6 SOFT-80%] spender=team=free-tier spend=21/25 tokens (84%) node=standalone
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z WARN  gatewayd::budget] [gb6 HARD-CAP] spender=team=free-tier spend=25/25 tokens (100%) node=standalone
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z ERROR gatewayd::proxy] [gb5 /openai] team=free-tier EXCEEDED mid-stream: spent 28/25 tokens; CUTTING the stream with the GB-4 terminal event cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z INFO  gatewayd::budget] [budget /openai] team=free-tier no usage frame; spent=28/25 tokens (share=25, estimate stands) [CUT] cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z INFO  gatewayd::proxy] [gb5 /openai] team=free-tier DENIED at admission: spent 28/25 tokens (rejecting: missing_attribution) cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:09Z INFO  gatewayd::proxy] [gb5 /openai] team=free-tier DENIED at admission: spent 28/25 tokens (rejecting: missing_attribution) cfg=v1

--------------------------------------------------------------
(4) GB-5 MID-STREAM CUT with the GB-4 terminal event
--------------------------------------------------------------
A 3-token cap is exhausted MID-generation. The stream is cut with the
operator's terminal event (event: error / data: budget_exhausted); the
upstream's [DONE] never reaches the client — the stream did not run to
completion.

$ curl -sN -X POST 'http://127.0.0.1:6188/openai/v1/chat' -H 'x-attr-team: ml-research' -d '{}'
data: {"id":"chatcmpl-spike1","object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"gpt-4.1","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-spike1","object":"chat.completion.chunk","model":"gpt-4.1","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"The Gateway"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

event: error
data: {"error":"budget_exhausted","spender":"team=ml-research","cap_tokens":3,"spend_tokens":7}


gatewayd log: the mid-stream cut and the reconciled terminal count:
    [2026-08-01T19:13:10Z ERROR gatewayd::proxy] [gb5 /openai] team=ml-research EXCEEDED mid-stream: spent 7/3 tokens; CUTTING the stream with the GB-4 terminal event cfg=v1
    [2026-08-01T19:13:10Z INFO  gatewayd::budget] [budget /openai] team=ml-research no usage frame; spent=7/3 tokens (share=3, estimate stands) [CUT] cfg=v1

--------------------------------------------------------------
(5) GB-5 BOUNDED OVERSPEND UNDER PARTITION — the MEASURED number
--------------------------------------------------------------
When a node cannot reach the control plane it fails to a DOCUMENTED
bounded-overspend policy: spend only up to the share it already holds,
then stop. A node holding a 40k share of a 100k cap admits one last stream
and is cut at its share + that stream's tail. The overspend is MEASURED —
reported as a number against the configured cap, never estimated:

NOTE: unlike scenarios 1-4 (which drive the real gatewayd over HTTP), this
number comes from executing the enforcement unit (LocalBudget) under a
SIMULATED partition — real code, real measurement, no gRPC round trip:
$ cargo test -q -p gatewayd --bin gatewayd budget::tests::measured_bounded_overspend_under_partition -- --nocapture 2>/dev/null | grep MEASURED
[MEASURED] partition bounded-overspend: cap=100000 tokens, held_share=40000, spent=41600, overspend=1600 tokens (1.60% of the cap); the node was UNREACHABLE and stopped at its share + one stream's tail, never unbounded

Bounded: the overspend is one stream's tail past the held share, strictly
less than one request's worth — never the unbounded local-bucket failure
(docs/01 Q4; docs/02 'GB-5 at fleet scale — budget shares').

==============================================================
 Phase 3 demo complete. GB-5 caps enforced, GB-6 alerts fired,
 mid-stream cut with the GB-4 terminal event, partition
 overspend MEASURED as a number against the cap.
==============================================================
